      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(replay): strip stale thinking blocks on replay_invalid signature errors",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #99654\n\nWhen `thinkingDefault` is changed from 'adaptive' to 'off' across a gateway restart, sessions with persisted signed thinking blocks fail with `replay_invalid` on every subsequent call. The existing retry loop fires 3x on the same unchanged history — all three rejected identically.\n\n## Change\n\nThis change detects thinking-signature `replay_invalid` errors (matching both `thinking` and `invalid/expired signature` patterns in the error message) and strips thinking blocks from session history using the existing `dropThinkingBlocks` utility before retrying once immediately. This matches the approach already used by the compaction replay path (`stripStaleThinkingSignaturesForCompactionReplay`).\n\n- Only retries once for this specific error (guarded by instance flag `replayInvalidThinkingStripped`)\n- Does not count against the normal retry budget\n- Skips backoff delay since the fix is deterministic (strip and retry)\n- Normal retryable errors (rate limits, 5xx, etc.) are unaffected\n\n## Files changed\n\n- `src/agents/sessions/agent-session.ts` (+60 lines)\n\n## Testing\n\n- `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/thinking.test.ts` — all 50 tests pass\n- `src/llm/utils/retry.test.ts` — all 6 tests pass\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
